{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FXtAVH38WJc8vy57eXD1pG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, based on the \"best\" tier definition they provided. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and predict results consistent with the best tier narrative.\n\nThe best tier means:\n- CIVO mechanism generalizes cleanly across environments\n- Dual-pathway finding strengthens diagnostic depth\n- TAWM contrast is compelling\n\nCore hypotheses for best tier:\n1. Cheetah Run trained dt_emb → nve>1.5x in ≥2/3 seeds (CIVO replicates)\n\n\n2. Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb → nve>1.5x in ≥2/3 seeds\n3. NVE 1.5x threshold maintains ≥90% classification accuracy cross-environment (≥11/12 correct)\n4. No concurrent publication demonstrates successful dt-conditioning in imagination-based AC before CoRL deadline\n5. Dual-pathway finding (Pathway A CIVO + Pathway B policy instability) characterizable with distinct signatures across environments\n6. Full-SGS (exp_018) shows meaningful intervention effect on observation-decoder gradient pathway\n\nNow I'm laying out the expected metric ranges for each environment and condition to ground the predicted data generation. I'm cross-referencing the experiment plan against the registry to see which ones are actually still pending. Plan 011 and 014 show as completed despite being marked planned, while 012 has mixed results with one killed run. Plan 013 appears to be the only one genuinely awaiting execution.\n\nLooking at the broader set of planned experiments, I see several Cheetah Run variants (baseline, trained embeddings, zero embedding dimension, untrained embeddings) and Cartpole Swingup tests all queued up, along with analysis tasks for RSSM fidelity, actor entropy, value prediction distributions, and embedding similarity metrics.\n\nBut I'm noticing some of these experiments are already marked as done in the registry—specifically plan_015 with the frozen dt_emb showing negative results due to gradient starvation, and plan_030 with the RSSM fidelity analysis. I need to reconcile which experiments are actually still pending versus which have already completed.\n\nLooking at the plan status field directly, I should predict results for all experiments marked as \"planned\" that haven't been cancelled, even if some registry entries suggest they've already run. Let me go through the planned ones systematically and start making predictions for each. I'm seeing the rest of the experiment list, and now I need to generate detailed predictions for each planned experiment. Since the user is asking for the \"imagined\" best-tier dataset, I should provide predicted data even for experiments that already have registry entries, keeping everything consistent with what CIVO would achieve. Let me structure this as a comprehensive YAML output covering all the planned experiments with their predicted results and rationales. Cheetah and Cartpole both show nve>1.5x with trained dt_emb - dual-pathway signatures appear in both environments with clean architectural distinctions between CIVO and policy instability patterns.\n\nFor plan_011, both seeds exceed the nve threshold with a collapse rate within expected range. Plan_012 confirms causal control with both seeds staying below nve 1.5x. Plan_014 shows the dual-pathway finding again with one seed succeeding and one collapsing. Plan_013 needs untrained dt_emb prediction - expecting value suppression below 1.0x with recovery behavior. Plan_020 is running with Cheetah baseline showing a peak around 732.9, targeting a final score near 800.\n\nNow looking at the Cheetah trained dt_emb results - 2 or 3 seeds exceed nve>1.5x with collapses in 1-2 seeds and eval degradation of 35-70%. The dt_embed_dim=0 variant shows 0/3 seeds exceeding threshold, confirming causal control. Untrained dt_emb suppresses nve below 1.0x with similar recovery to Walker. Cartpole experiments replicate the same pattern across environments, and I'm examining nve threshold sensitivity next.\n\nThe 1.5x threshold achieves ≥90% accuracy with AUROC > 0.95. Frozen dt_emb confirms trained embeddings are necessary. Additional seeds from 008e_v3 show about 50% collapse rate overall. Full-SGS intervention meaningfully delays or prevents CIVO onset with lower nve peaks. RSSM analysis shows clear fidelity gap between dt2 and dt1, and actor entropy diverges sharply in collapsed configs.\n\nValue predictions show bimodal distributions in collapsed cases, while dt embeddings diverge during training correlating with collapse onset. Uncertainty-gated truncation shows promise as partial mitigation, and Hopper Hop confirms generalization holds.\n\nNow I'm compiling baseline performance numbers for Cheetah Run — DreamerV3 typically converges around 800-900, and the current experiment peaked at 732.9 at 265K steps which is still climbing, so I'm estimating a final mean of roughly 820 across the seeds.\n\nWith dt embedding training, I'm expecting the best tier to show nve peaks between 1.6 and 3.5 with eval degradation of 35-70% compared to baseline, which would put performance somewhere in the 246-533 range if baseline is around 820 — probably peaking near 450 before some collapse occurs. For Cartpole Swingup, the baseline should converge similarly to around 800-860, and I'd expect the trained dt_emb to follow the same CIVO pattern.\n\nI'm noticing that plan_018 (Full-SGS) appears in the framing and is currently running in the registry, but it's not explicitly listed in the planned experiments, so I need to clarify whether to include it based on the user's request for \"planned\" status entries.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40578,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m